                  "text": "Mars slows\u2026 and stops. First Stationary Point.",
                  "color": [
                    255,
                    200,
                    80,
                    255
                  ],
                  "fontSize": 28,
                  "wrapText": false
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "changeMeaning": "Mars moves eastward to its central position in Virgo, then appears to pause, representing the moment of stationary point before retrograde begins. A text label highlights this reversal point.",
          "narration": "But every 26 months, something strange happens. Mars gradually slows its eastward crawl, stops, and then \u2014 remarkably \u2014 begins moving westward, back toward Leo. Ancient astronomers found this deeply puzzling. Why would a celestial body reverse course?"
        },
        {
          "clipName": "clip2",
          "audioClip": "nightsky_retrograde_loop_traced",
          "autoAdvance": false,
          "changes": [
